# Agent-configuration namespaces (.air/ and .junie/) are left fully visible to Git
# by default.
#
# Do NOT ignore the whole .air/ or .junie/ namespaces, nor their plan directories:
# both may contain durable, shareable project artifacts that are intended to be
# versioned (e.g. worktree setup, Docker environment, MCP configuration, and review
# prompts under .air/; Skills and other project-scoped agent configuration under
# .junie/). Air plan files may be useful project artifacts, and Junie plans are
# explicitly designed to be editable/committable.
#
# Generated does not imply transient: do not add ignore rules for tool-owned
# namespaces or generated artifacts without concrete evidence about their lifecycle
# and repository value. Default to visibility/versionability when uncertain; ignore
# only paths demonstrated to be local/session-only and not useful for collaboration,
# provenance, replay, or review.
